     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one dose is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **500 mg** three times daily (1,500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg** three times daily (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg total per day**, split into doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nTell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate and why. I'll enter the order once that's settled."
      }
